<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav April copper output rises.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav April copper output rises.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES     APRIL	MARCH	APRIL1996</p>
<p> copper (thousand tonnes)	1,811	1,781	 1,554</p>
<p> lead-zinc				78	   73	    72</p>
<p> bauxite				  10	   45	    12</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes)  9,379	9,362	 4,401</p>
<p> refined lead			1,847	  527	 2,176</p>
<p> zinc				  2,320	3,120	 2,065</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		  6,306	4,876	 3,101</p>
<p> refined silver (kilos)	  3,949	4,481	 3,208</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 311 4254</p>
</text>
